    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d629">

                <pb facs="0839" n="763" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg763"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.5431/234</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Swiss Chargé</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Micheli</hi>)</head>
                <p>The Secretary of State presents his compliments to the Chargé d’Affaires ad
                    interim of Switzerland and has the honor to refer to his note of September 11,
                    1935, in regard to the question of the possible extension beyond October 1,
                    1935, of the time during which the customs duties proclaimed in connection with
                    the trade agreements with Belgium, Haiti and Sweden will be applied to products
                    originating in Switzerland or Liechtenstein. This question has been considered
                    most carefully and sympathetically.</p>
                <p>The Chargé d’Affaires ad interim is informed that in view of the fact that the
                    negotiations looking toward a trade agreement between <pb facs="0840" n="764"
                        xml:id="pg764"/> the United States and Switzerland are still in progress and
                    give promise of being brought to a successful conclusion in the near future, it
                    is expected that the President, at a very early date, will instruct the
                    Secretary of the Treasury to continue for a specified time to apply the
                    above-mentioned duties to Swiss products.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1935-09-17">September 17,
                            1935</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
